  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets an 8% cap with no sales stop and no transition, letting the Hearth 10 (6.2%) remain on sale, while per-model results go to customers and regulators but not the public. S5 makes exceedance of 8 per 100,000 a mandatory recall, but lets the regulator approve an open-ended corrective alternative, which substantially weakens the trigger for the Ember 8 (9.9). S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 36 months, within the 6-year retrofit window, which favours Northwind's 38% coverage."
